    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="cea83ff3-eadc-5977-bce6-cb14ee4f9662" activityNameId="46c1fe16-c988-5f4a-8eea-4bd777e2a5d0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Radioactive waste, in final repository for nuclear waste LLW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Radioactive waste, in final repository for nuclear waste LLW
For operation is meant the input of the waste and the refilling of the tunnels. The waste volume includes always the container. The density of ILW is approximately 2.5 tonne per m3. The total electricity supplied from the grid has been estimated from information on the power and the duration of operations given for the early design of a Swiss LAW repository, adjusted to the new waste inventory. For the transport of the radioactive waste, an average distance of 100 km has been considered. The burdens associated with this repository are allocated to the total amount of radioactive waste, mostly produced by nuclear power plants, but also by medicine and industry.;
Synonyms: Low and intermediate level long-lived radioactive waste; 
UUID: 0004e814-c18d-42e2-a3f7-ce1fa51a3c2c
This module includes: concrete and energy requirements; transports of radioactive waste and concrete; infrastructure requirement; methan emissions to air; and, seepage water treatement. This describes the operation of a repository for intermediate and long-lived low radioactive waste in the Swiss context.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Currently available knowledge.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0004e814-c18d-42e2-a3f7-ce1fa51a3c2c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
